Z||000000||Kasdan||11-20-2001||04:52 PM||||Will the turbocharger off a volvo fit?  I can get my hands on 1 or 2 and id like to use them  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Tyler Morgan, 1986 GT<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/kassig2.gif">                  <BR>Aftermarket Power Steering, Rebuilt 2.8<BR>http://www.geocities.com/mtyler14/index.html||||reg||1
Z||000001||Turbo88||11-20-2001||05:14 PM||||The easiest way to match a turbo to a car without doing all the math is to get a turbo off an engine that is close to the same displacement and redline. Generally, the smaller the engine, the smaller the turbo. It will restrict exhaust flow more and will want to spin too fast. If it comes off a larger engine, it will have more "lag" and will not want to come into boost as fast. If I had to come up with a rule of thumb, all things being equal, try to stay within .5 lt or so..  ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Kasdan||11-20-2001||05:17 PM||||do they make a volvo motor around 2.8 liters?  it could come off a motor anywhere from 2.3-3.3 liters...<P>------------------<BR>Tyler Morgan, 1986 GT<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/kassig2.gif">                  <BR>Aftermarket Power Steering, Rebuilt 2.8<BR>http://www.geocities.com/mtyler14/index.html||||reg||1
Z||000003||Kasdan||11-21-2001||07:55 AM||||bump||||reg||1
Z||000004||Turbo88||11-21-2001||09:54 AM||||I don't know about Volvo motors but yes, roughly speaking, I would say anything between 2.3 and 3.3 should do fine. If you are getting a salvage turbo, I strongly advise rebuilding it. Make sure is spins freely and there is no play in the shaft.||||reg||1
Z||000005||peterh||11-21-2001||10:47 AM||||I have a 1988 Volvoo 740 with a 2.4 liter 4cyl engine with 207,000 miles on original engine and turbo. It is a 2.3Liter I believe. It makes about 160hp. My wifes car is a 1994 850 turbo 2.3L 5 cylinder dohc that puts out 220HP. Note: Both of these are water intercooled. Do an internet search for volvo speed sites (www.brickboard.com is one for more info on turbos on volvos). Hope this helps.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000006||peterh||11-21-2001||10:51 AM||||PS.<BR>Another good site is <A HREF="http://www.turbobricks.org" TARGET=_blank>www.turbobricks.org</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000007||Wannabe||11-21-2001||08:21 PM||||Another good trick you will find expained on the Turbobricks site is how to adapt a mid '80s Saab electronic boost control with knock sensor. A neat low buck trick.||||reg||1
